The user pictures offered by the installer.

Taken unchanged from GNOME's gnome-control-center, which ships them at
/usr/share/pixmaps/faces:

    https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-control-center
    GPL-2.0-or-later

Photographs of objects rather than drawings of people, which is the whole
reason for preferring them: a cartoon face is a picture of somebody who is
not you, and the illustrated sets shipped by desktops tend to read as a
child's avatar picker. A bicycle does not claim to be anybody.
